                            <comment id="16650032" author="andrey-kuznetsov" created="Mon, 15 Oct 2018 10:27:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, could you please review the change &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; ?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4962&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4962&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16650569" author="agura" created="Mon, 15 Oct 2018 18:22:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=andrey-kuznetsov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;andrey-kuznetsov&quot;&gt;andrey-kuznetsov&lt;/a&gt; I&apos;ve found a mistake a-la copy&amp;amp;paste. See upsource comments.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16651305" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 16 Oct 2018 08:24:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=andrey-kuznetsov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;andrey-kuznetsov&quot;&gt;andrey-kuznetsov&lt;/a&gt;, in my opinion, such approach to caches start defeats the purpose of the watchdog service. All potentially dangerous operations are now wrapped in &lt;tt&gt;blockingSectionBegin/blockingSectionEnd&lt;/tt&gt;. Instead, we should insert thread progress markers to all loops where we iterate over caches (for example, inside &lt;tt&gt;forAllRegisteredCacheGroups&lt;/tt&gt;) and over partitions. This way we will still report a long-running disk IO operations, but will tolerate a large number of starting caches.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16651936" author="andrey-kuznetsov" created="Tue, 16 Oct 2018 15:34:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, thanks for your comments. I&apos;ve made all required changes. I had to update progress marker for exchanger worker from threads other than exchanger thread. Are you ok with this? &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TeamCity (re)tests are in progress right now.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16652439" author="andrey-kuznetsov" created="Tue, 16 Oct 2018 21:08:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;TeamCity tests were passed successfully.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16653243" author="agoncharuk" created="Wed, 17 Oct 2018 09:25:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=andrey-kuznetsov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;andrey-kuznetsov&quot;&gt;andrey-kuznetsov&lt;/a&gt; I think we can merge this version for 2.7, and I will think a little bit more how we can reduce the number of the blocking sections in exchange future.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
